{
 "manufacturer": "Finder",
 "manufacturer_slug": "finder",
 "model": "7M.24 single-phase energy meter (Modbus RS485)",
 "model_slug": "7m24",
 "short_model": "7M.24",
 "aliases": [
  "7M.24",
  "7M24",
  "Finder 7M24 Modbus"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
 "applies_to": "Finder 7M.24 single-phase meters with RS485 communication, per the 7M24 section of 'Modbus Communication Protocol 7M24 - 7M38' v2.",
 "summary": "The 7M.24 is Finder's single-phase MID energy meter for DIN rail. The RS485 version answers Modbus RTU and offers its measurements both in packed integer formats and as IEEE 754 floats. This map uses the float block (voltage, current, powers, power factor, THD, frequency, energy counters) plus identification, status, tariff, reset and serial-port registers.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "Modicon",
  "note": "Registers are printed as 3xxxx (input, function 04) and 4xxxx (holding, functions 03/06/16) with 30000 / 40000 as the memory reference, not 30001. The document's request example reads U1 (30107) by sending start address 0x006B = 107. Wire address = printed number minus 30000 or 40000: Pt float 32490 is input register 2490."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Modbus Communication Protocol 7M24 - 7M38",
  "doc_number": "v2",
  "revision_date": "2021-06-30",
  "url": "https://cdn.findernet.com/app/uploads/Modbus-7M24-7M38_v2_30062021.pdf",
  "pages": "Addressing example p. 3; 7M24 input registers pp. 5-10, holding registers pp. 11-21, data types pp. 22-23 (printed page numbers)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Wire address = printed number - 30000 (input) or - 40000 (holding); see the 30107 / 0x006B example.",
  "T_float is IEEE 754 single precision, high word first (ABCD); the data-type page's example stores 123.45 as 42F6 E666. T3 (signed 32-bit) is also high word first.",
  "Left out: the integer measurement block (T5/T6/T7 packed exponent formats), the mantissa/exponent energy counters and the '1000 x energy counter' block, as for the 7M.38 map.",
  "Left out: duplicate float rows (a second Pt/Qt/St/PFt/frequency set at 32536-32584 and float counters n1-n4 at 32638-32645 without a function code), CAP/IND power factor floats (sign convention not explained), and the alarm, logic, LCD, data-logger and other configuration groups.",
  "Energy counters 1-8 are user counters reset through 40031; what each one integrates is set in its parameter/configuration registers (40421 onward), so check the assignment on the meter.",
  "Writing settings needs the access level raised by writing the user password to 40001-40002 (function 16), then saving with operator command 40012 = 1."
 ],
